ue,"LatexCode":"\\frac{11}{12}"}],"StageId":1,"Question":{"Ar":"أي الكُسور التالية أقرب إلى العدد 1؟","En":"Which fraction is closest to 1?"},"Solution":{"Idea":{"Ar":"الأقرب إلى الواحد هو صاحب أصغر مسافة مطلقة عنه.","En":"The closest value to one has the smallest absolute distance from it."},"Unit":{"Ar":"بلا وحدة قياس","En":"Dimensionless"},"Steps":[{"Ar":"جميع الخيارات أصغر من واحد، فنحسب المسافة بطرح كل كسر من واحد.","En":"All choices are below one, so subtract each fraction from one to find its distance."},{"Ar":"المسافات بالترتيب $\\frac1{10},\\frac3{16},\\frac18,\\frac1{12}$.","En":"The distances in order are $\\frac1{10},\\frac3{16},\\frac18,\\frac1{12}$."},{"Ar":"أصغرها $\\frac1{12}$، لذا الخيار الرابع أقرب إلى واحد.","En":"The smallest is $\\frac1{12}$, making the fourth option closest to one."}],"Result":{"Ar":"$\\frac{11}{12}$","En":"$\\frac{11}{12}$"},"CommonError":{"Ar":"قارن المسافات لا المقامات وحدها.","En":"Compare distances, not denominators alone."},"FormulaLatex":"d(x,1)=|1-x|","Substitution":{"Ar":"$\\frac1{12}<\\frac1{10}<\\frac18<\\frac3{16}$","En":"$\\frac1{12}<\\frac1{10}<\\frac18<\\frac3{16}$"},"Verification":{"Ar":"بالمقام المشترك 240 تصبح المسافات 24 و45 و30 و20 جزءاً من 240؛ الأصغر 20.","En":"With denominator 240, distances have numerators 24, 45, 30 and 20; 20 is smallest."}},"TrackIds":[5],"CategoryId":21,"PrimarySkillId":112,"DifficultyLevel":1,"SecondarySkillIds":[]}$mw$::jsonb,$mw${"DifficultyLevel":1,"Hints":[{"Ar":"فكر في المسافة بين كل كسر والواحد.","En":"Think about the distance of each fraction from one."},{"Ar":"اطرح كل خيار من الواحد وقارن الفروق.","En":"Subtract each option from one and compare the differences."}],"Solution":{"Idea":{"Ar":"الأقرب إلى الواحد هو صاحب أصغر مسافة مطلقة عنه.","En":"The closest value to one has the smallest absolute distance from it."},"Unit":{"Ar":"بلا وحدة قياس","En":"Dimensionless"},"Steps":[{"Ar":"جميع الخيارات أصغر من واحد، فنحسب المسافة بطرح كل كسر من واحد.","En":"All choices are below one, so subtract each fraction from one to find its distance."},{"Ar":"المسافات بالترتيب $\\frac1{10},\\frac3{16},\\frac18,\\frac1{12}$.","En":"The distances in order are $\\frac1{10},\\frac3{16},\\frac18,\\frac1{12}$."},{"Ar":"أصغرها $\\frac1{12}$، لذا الخيار الرابع أقرب إلى واحد.","En":"The smallest is $\\frac1{12}$, making the fourth option closest to one."}],"Result":{"Ar":"$\\frac{11}{12}$","En":"$\\frac{11}{12}$"},"CommonError":{"Ar":"قارن المسافات لا المقامات وحدها.","En":"Compare distances, not denominators alone."},"FormulaLatex":"d(x,1)=|1-x|","Substitution":{"Ar":"$\\frac1{12}<\\frac1{10}<\\frac18<\\frac3{16}$","En":"$\\frac1{12}<\\frac1{10}<\\frac18<\\frac3{16}$"},"Verification":{"Ar":"بالمقام المشترك 240 تصبح المسافات 24 و45 و30 و20 جزءاً من 240؛ الأصغر 20.","En":"With denominator 240, distances have numerators 24, 45, 30 and 20; 20 is smallest."}},"Distractors":[{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"المسافة 1/10 أكبر من 1/12.","En":"Distance 1/10 exceeds 1/12."},"Order":1},{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"المسافة 3/16 أكبر من 1/12.","En":"Distance 3/16 exceeds 1/12."},"Order":2},{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"المسافة 1/8 أكبر من 1/12.","En":"Distance 1/8 exceeds 1/12."},"Order":3},{"ErrorType":"","Reason":null,"Order":4}]}$mw$,$mw$الأقرب إلى الواحد هو صاحب أصغر مسافة مطلقة عنه.

$d(x,1)=|1-x|$

1. جميع الخيارات أصغر من واحد، فنحسب المسافة بطرح كل كسر من واحد.

2. المسافات بالترتيب $\frac1{10},\frac3{16},\frac18,\frac1{12}$.

3. أصغرها $\frac1{12}$، لذا الخيار الرابع أقرب إلى واحد.

$\frac1{12}<\frac1{10}<\frac18<\frac3{16}$

$\frac{11}{12}$ بلا وحدة قياس

بالمقام المشترك 240 تصبح المسافات 24 و45 و30 و20 جزءاً من 240؛ الأصغر 20.

قارن المسافات لا المقامات وحدها.$mw$,$mw$The closest value to one has the smallest absolute distance from it.

$d(x,1)=|1-x|$

1. All choices are below one, so subtract each fraction from one to find its distance.

2. The distances in order are $\frac1{10},\frac3{16},\frac18,\frac1{12}$.

3. The smallest is $\frac1{12}$, making the fourth option closest to one.

$\frac1{12}<\frac1{10}<\frac18<\frac3{16}$

$\frac{11}{12}$ Dimensionless

With denominator 240, distances have numerators 24, 45, 30 and 20; 20 is smallest.

Compare distances, not denominators alone.$mw$),
(650,506,$mw$BCE2E07B67116A38E9EAA6D5BF14E644A1590BAF153F36E977E60ECF9DB5B846$mw$,$mw$beed0bd5c7e0ae9015dc8e7117e3ca58$mw$,$mw$$mw$,$mw${"Id":506,"StageId":1,"CategoryId":21,"Points":10,"TitleAr":"تحديد كسر بين كسرين على مستقيم الأعداد","TitleEn":"Identify a fraction strictly between two fractions","QuestionTextAr":"أي كسر يقع بين $\\frac13$ و$\\frac12$ دون أن يساوي أيّاً منهما؟","QuestionTextEn":"Which fraction lies strictly between $\\frac13$ and $\\frac12$?","DetailedSolutionAr":"نحوّل إلى مقام 12: $\\frac13=\\frac4{12}$ و$\\frac12=\\frac6{12}$. إذن $\\frac5{12}$ بينهما.","DetailedSolutionEn":"With denominator 12: $\\frac13=\\frac4{12}$ and $\\frac12=\\frac6{12}$. The fraction $\\frac5{12}$ lies between them.","YoutubeSolutionUrl":null,"EditorialDetailsJson":null,"Options":[{"Id":2013,"Order":1,"LatexCode":"\\frac14","IsCorrect":false},{"Id":2014,"Order":2,"LatexCode":"\\frac5{12}","IsCorrect":true},{"Id":2015,"Order":3,"LatexCode":"\\frac35","IsCorrect":false},{"Id":2016,"Order":4,"LatexCode":"\\frac12","IsCorrect":false}]}$mw$::jsonb,$mw${"Hints":[{"Ar":"كلمة بين هنا تستثني الطرفين.","En":"Between here excludes both endpoints."},{"Ar":"اكتب الحدين بمقام مشترك ثم اختبر كل خيار بالمتباينتين الصارمتين.","En":"Write the bounds with a common denominator, then test each choice against both strict inequalities."}],"Title":{"Ar":"تحديد كسر بين كسرين على مستقيم الأعداد","En":"Identify a fraction strictly between two fractions"},"Points":10,"Options":[{"Reason":{"Ar":"1/4 أصغر من 1/3.","En":"1/4 is below 1/3."},"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","IsCorrect":false,"LatexCode":"\\frac14"},{"Reason":null,"ErrorType":"","IsCorrect":true,"LatexCode":"\\frac5{12}"},{"Reason":{"Ar":"3/5 أكبر من 1/2.","En":"3/5 is above 1/2."},"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","IsCorrect":false,"LatexCode":"\\frac35"},{"Reason":{"Ar":"1/2 هو الحد الأعلى المستبعد.","En":"1/2 is the excluded upper endpoint."},"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","IsCorrect":false,"LatexCode":"\\frac12"}],"StageId":1,"Question":{"Ar":"أي كسر يقع بين $\\frac13$ و$\\frac12$ دون أن يساوي أيّاً منهما؟","En":"Which fraction lies strictly between $\\frac13$ and $\\frac12$?"},"Solution":{"Idea":{"Ar":"الكسر داخل فترة مفتوحة يجب أن يكون أكبر من الحد الأدنى وأصغر من الحد الأعلى.","En":"A fraction in an open interval must be strictly greater than the lower bound and strictly less than the upper bound."},"Unit":{"Ar":"بلا وحدة قياس","En":"Dimensionless"},"Steps":[{"Ar":"نكتب الحدين $\\frac13=\\frac4{12}$ و$\\frac12=\\frac6{12}$.","En":"Rewrite the bounds as $\\frac13=\\frac4{12}$ and $\\frac12=\\frac6{12}$."},{"Ar":"يقع البسط 5 بين 4 و6 تماماً؛ إذن $\\frac4{12}<\\frac5{12}<\\frac6{12}$.","En":"Numerator 5 is strictly between 4 and 6, so $\\frac4{12}<\\frac5{12}<\\frac6{12}$."}],"Result":{"Ar":"$\\frac5{12}$","En":"$\\frac5{12}$"},"CommonError":{"Ar":"المتباينة الصارمة لا تشمل طرفي الفترة.","En":"Strict inequalities exclude the endpoints."},"FormulaLatex":"\\frac13<x<\\frac12","Substitution":{"Ar":"$\\frac4{12}<\\frac5{12}<\\frac6{12}$","En":"$\\frac4{12}<\\frac5{12}<\\frac6{12}$"},"Verification":{"Ar":"$\\frac5{12}-\\frac13=\\frac1{12},\\quad\\frac12-\\frac5{12}=\\frac1{12}$","En":"$\\frac5{12}-\\frac13=\\frac1{12},\\quad\\frac12-\\frac5{12}=\\frac1{12}$"}},"TrackIds":[5],"CategoryId":21,"PrimarySkillId":112,"DifficultyLevel":1,"SecondarySkillIds":[]}$mw$::jsonb,$mw${"DifficultyLevel":1,"Hints":[{"Ar":"كلمة بين هنا تستثني الطرفين.","En":"Between here excludes both endpoints."},{"Ar":"اكتب الحدين بمقام مشترك ثم اختبر كل خيار بالمتباينتين الصارمتين.","En":"Write the bounds with a common denominator, then test each choice against both strict inequalities."}],"Solution":{"Idea":{"Ar":"الكسر داخل فترة مفتوحة يجب أن يكون أكبر من الحد الأدنى وأصغر من الحد الأعلى.","En":"A fraction in an open interval must be strictly greater than the lower bound and strictly less than the upper bound."},"Unit":{"Ar":"بلا وحدة قياس","En":"Dimensionless"},"Steps":[{"Ar":"نكتب الحدين $\\frac13=\\frac4{12}$ و$\\frac12=\\frac6{12}$.","En":"Rewrite the bounds as $\\frac13=\\frac4{12}$ and $\\frac12=\\frac6{12}$."},{"Ar":"يقع البسط 5 بين 4 و6 تماماً؛ إذن $\\frac4{12}<\\frac5{12}<\\frac6{12}$.","En":"Numerator 5 is strictly between 4 and 6, so $\\frac4{12}<\\frac5{12}<\\frac6{12}$."}],"Result":{"Ar":"$\\frac5{12}$","En":"$\\frac5{12}$"},"CommonError":{"Ar":"المتباينة الصارمة لا تشمل طرفي الفترة.","En":"Strict inequalities exclude the endpoints."},"FormulaLatex":"\\frac13<x<\\frac12","Substitution":{"Ar":"$\\frac4{12}<\\frac5{12}<\\frac6{12}$","En":"$\\frac4{12}<\\frac5{12}<\\frac6{12}$"},"Verification":{"Ar":"$\\frac5{12}-\\frac13=\\frac1{12},\\quad\\frac12-\\frac5{12}=\\frac1{12}$","En":"$\\frac5{12}-\\frac13=\\frac1{12},\\quad\\frac12-\\frac5{12}=\\frac1{12}$"}},"Distractors":[{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"1/4 أصغر من 1/3.","En":"1/4 is below 1/3."},"Order":1},{"ErrorType":"","Reason":null,"Order":2},{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"3/5 أكبر من 1/2.","En":"3/5 is above 1/2."},"Order":3},{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"1/2 هو الحد الأعلى المستبعد.","En":"1/2 is the excluded upper endpoint."},"Order":4}]}$mw$,$mw$الكسر داخل فترة مفتوحة يجب أن يكون أكبر من الحد الأدنى وأصغر من الحد الأعلى.

$\frac13<x<\frac12$

1. نكتب الحدين $\frac13=\frac4{12}$ و$\frac12=\frac6{12}$.

2. يقع البسط 5 بين 4 و6 تماماً؛ إذن $\frac4{12}<\frac5{12}<\frac6{12}$.

$\frac4{12}<\frac5{12}<\frac6{12}$

$\frac5{12}$ بلا وحدة قياس

$\frac5{12}-\frac13=\frac1{12},\quad\frac12-\frac5{12}=\frac1{12}$

المتباينة الصارمة لا تشمل طرفي الفترة.$mw$,$mw$A fraction in an open interval must be strictly greater than the lower bound and strictly less than the upper bound.

$\frac13<x<\frac12$

1. Rewrite the bounds as $\frac13=\frac4{12}$ and $\frac12=\frac6{12}$.

2. Numerator 5 is strictly between 4 and 6, so $\frac4{12}<\frac5{12}<\frac6{12}$.

$\frac4{12}<\frac5{12}<\frac6{12}$

$\frac5{12}$ Dimensionless

$\frac5{12}-\frac13=\frac1{12},\quad\frac12-\frac5{12}=\frac1{12}$

Strict inequalities exclude the endpoints.$mw$),
(652,508,$mw$602C9DB367EC20174E0FEC5350D7EA00936BABDF47BC6F9947BE3407D514FCA0$mw$,$mw$95ee193618ca20637ac60af36b7562e9$mw$,$mw$$mw$,$mw${"Id":508,"StageId":3,"CategoryId":23,"Points":10,"TitleAr":"حساب مجموع متسلسلة هندسية متناوبة متقاربة","TitleEn":"Find the sum of a convergent alternating geometric series","QuestionTextAr":"ما مجموع المتسلسلة اللانهائية $1-\\frac12+\\frac14-\\frac18+\\cdots$؟","QuestionTextEn":"What is the sum of $1-\\frac12+\\frac14-\\frac18+\\cdots$?","DetailedSolutionAr":"متسلسلة هندسية حدها الأول 1 ونسبتها $-\\frac12$ وقيمة النسبة المطلقة أقل من 1، إذن $S=\\frac1{1-(-1/2)}=\\frac23$.","DetailedSolutionEn":"This is geometric with first term 1 and ratio $-\\frac12$, whose absolute value is below 1. Thus $S=\\frac1{1-(-1/2)}=\\frac23$.","YoutubeSolutionUrl":null,"EditorialDetailsJson":null,"Options":[{"Id":2021,"Order":1,"LatexCode":"\\frac12","IsCorrect":false},{"Id":2022,"Order":2,"LatexCode":"\\frac23","IsCorrect":true},{"Id":2023,"Order":3,"LatexCode":"\\frac32","IsCorrect":false},{"Id":2024,"Order":4,"LatexCode":"1","IsCorrect":false}]}$mw$::jsonb,$mw${"Hints":[{"Ar":"حدد النسبة مع إشارتها.","En":"Determine the signed common ratio."},{"Ar":"عوّض في صيغة المجموع الهندسي المتقارب.","En":"Substitute into the convergent geometric sum formula."}],"Title":{"Ar":"حساب مجموع متسلسلة هندسية متناوبة متقاربة","En":"Find the sum of a convergent alternating geometric series"},"Points":10,"Options":[{"Reason":{"Ar":"1/2 مجموع أول حدين فقط.","En":"1/2 is the sum of only the first two terms."},"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","IsCorrect":false,"LatexCode":"\\frac12"},{"Reason":null,"ErrorType":"","IsCorrect":true,"LatexCode":"\\frac23"},{"Reason":{"Ar":"3/2 هو المقام بعد التبسيط، وليس حاصل القسمة.","En":"3/2 is the simplified denominator, not the quotient."},"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","IsCorrect":false,"LatexCode":"\\frac32"},{"Reason":{"Ar":"1 يهمل جميع الحدود بعد الحد الأول.","En":"1 ignores every term after the first."},"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","IsCorrect":false,"LatexCode":"1"}],"StageId":3,"Question":{"Ar":"ما مجموع المتسلسلة اللانهائية $1-\\frac12+\\frac14-\\frac18+\\cdots$؟","En":"What is the sum of $1-\\frac12+\\frac14-\\frac18+\\cdots$?"},"Solution":{"Idea":{"Ar":"المتسلسلة هندسية متناوبة ذات نسبة مطلقة أصغر من واحد.","En":"The alternating geometric series has absolute ratio below one."},"Unit":{"Ar":"بلا وحدة قياس","En":"Dimensionless"},"Steps":[{"Ar":"الحد الأول $a_1=1$ والنسبة المشتركة $r=-\\frac12$.","En":"The first term is $a_1=1$ and the common ratio is $r=-\\frac12$."},{"Ar":"شرط التقارب متحقق لأن $|r|=\\frac12<1$.","En":"The convergence condition holds because $|r|=\\frac12<1$."},{"Ar":"$S=\\frac1{1-(-1/2)}=\\frac1{3/2}=\\frac23$.","En":"$S=\\frac1{1-(-1/2)}=\\frac1{3/2}=\\frac23$."}],"Result":{"Ar":"$\\frac23$","En":"$\\frac23$"},"CommonError":{"Ar":"لا تهمل سالب النسبة.","En":"Do not omit the negative sign of the ratio."},"FormulaLatex":"S=\\frac{a_1}{1-r}\\quad(|r|<1)","Substitution":{"Ar":"$r=-1/2,\\quad S=\\frac1{1-(-1/2)}=\\frac23$","En":"$r=-1/2,\\quad S=\\frac1{1-(-1/2)}=\\frac23$"},"Verification":{"Ar":"$S+S/2=1$","En":"$S+S/2=1$"}},"TrackIds":[12],"CategoryId":23,"PrimarySkillId":113,"DifficultyLevel":1,"SecondarySkillIds":[]}$mw$::jsonb,$mw${"DifficultyLevel":1,"Hints":[{"Ar":"حدد النسبة مع إشارتها.","En":"Determine the signed common ratio."},{"Ar":"عوّض في صيغة المجموع الهندسي المتقارب.","En":"Substitute into the convergent geometric sum formula."}],"Solution":{"Idea":{"Ar":"المتسلسلة هندسية متناوبة ذات نسبة مطلقة أصغر من واحد.","En":"The alternating geometric series has absolute ratio below one."},"Unit":{"Ar":"بلا وحدة قياس","En":"Dimensionless"},"Steps":[{"Ar":"الحد الأول $a_1=1$ والنسبة المشتركة $r=-\\frac12$.","En":"The first term is $a_1=1$ and the common ratio is $r=-\\frac12$."},{"Ar":"شرط التقارب متحقق لأن $|r|=\\frac12<1$.","En":"The convergence condition holds because $|r|=\\frac12<1$."},{"Ar":"$S=\\frac1{1-(-1/2)}=\\frac1{3/2}=\\frac23$.","En":"$S=\\frac1{1-(-1/2)}=\\frac1{3/2}=\\frac23$."}],"Result":{"Ar":"$\\frac23$","En":"$\\frac23$"},"CommonError":{"Ar":"لا تهمل سالب النسبة.","En":"Do not omit the negative sign of the ratio."},"FormulaLatex":"S=\\frac{a_1}{1-r}\\quad(|r|<1)","Substitution":{"Ar":"$r=-1/2,\\quad S=\\frac1{1-(-1/2)}=\\frac23$","En":"$r=-1/2,\\quad S=\\frac1{1-(-1/2)}=\\frac23$"},"Verification":{"Ar":"$S+S/2=1$","En":"$S+S/2=1$"}},"Distractors":[{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"1/2 مجموع أول حدين فقط.","En":"1/2 is the sum of only the first two terms."},"Order":1},{"ErrorType":"","Reason":null,"Order":2},{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"3/2 هو المقام بعد التبسيط، وليس حاصل القسمة.","En":"3/2 is the simplified denominator, not the quotient."},"Order":3},{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"1 يهمل جميع الحدود بعد الحد الأول.","En":"1 ignores every term after the first."},"Order":4}]}$mw$,$mw$المتسلسلة هندسية متناوبة ذات نسبة مطلقة أصغر من واحد.

$S=\frac{a_1}{1-r}\quad(|r|<1)$

1. الحد الأول $a_1=1$ والنسبة المشتركة $r=-\frac12$.

2. شرط التقارب متحقق لأن $|r|=\frac12<1$.

3. $S=\frac1{1-(-1/2)}=\frac1{3/2}=\frac23$.

$r=-1/2,\quad S=\frac1{1-(-1/2)}=\frac23$

$\frac23$ بلا وحدة قياس

$S+S/2=1$

لا تهمل سالب النسبة.$mw$,$mw$The alternating geometric series has absolute ratio below one.

$S=\frac{a_1}{1-r}\quad(|r|<1)$

1. The first term is $a_1=1$ and the common ratio is $r=-\frac12$.

2. The convergence condition holds because $|r|=\frac12<1$.

3. $S=\frac1{1-(-1/2)}=\frac1{3/2}=\frac23$.

$r=-1/2,\quad S=\frac1{1-(-1/2)}=\frac23$

$\frac23$ Dimensionless

$S+S/2=1$

Do not omit the negative sign of the ratio.$mw$),
(653,509,$mw$31CFA3A1CC9E061D917FEA01BD64591C1C998E3D6FA6A1353888598377231084$mw$,$mw$02102ac8c4c97abacf1aed897130deb4$mw$,$mw$$mw$,$mw${"Id":509,"StageId":3,"CategoryId":23,"Points":10,"TitleAr":"تمييز التقارب وحساب المجموع النهائي","TitleEn":"Recognize convergence and calculate an infinite geometric sum","QuestionTextAr":"احسب مجموع المتسلسلة اللانهائية $6+2+\\frac23+\\frac29+\\cdots$.","QuestionTextEn":"Compute the infinite sum $6+2+\\frac23+\\frac29+\\cdots$.","DetailedSolutionAr":"القانون المستخدم: S = أ₁/(1−r) لمجموع متسلسلة هندسية لانهائية متقاربة حين |r| < 1. المتسلسلة 6 + 2 + 2/3 + 2/9 + ... حدها الأول 6 ونسبتها r = 2/6 = 1/3. بالتعويض: S = 6/(1−1/3) = 6/(2/3) = 9.","DetailedSolutionEn":"Rule used: The convergent geometric series sum is S=a₁/(1−r) for |r|<1. The series 6+2+2/3+2/9+... has first term 6 and ratio 2/6=1/3. Therefore S=6/(1−1/3)=6/(2/3)=9.","YoutubeSolutionUrl":null,"EditorialDetailsJson":null,"Options":[{"Id":2025,"Order":1,"LatexCode":"8","IsCorrect":false},{"Id":2026,"Order":2,"LatexCode":"9","IsCorrect":true},{"Id":2027,"Order":3,"LatexCode":"12","IsCorrect":false},{"Id":2028,"Order":4,"LatexCode":"18","IsCorrect":false}]}$mw$::jsonb,$mw${"Hints":[{"Ar":"استخرج النسبة بقسمة الثاني على الأول.","En":"Find the ratio by dividing the second term by the first."},{"Ar":"طبّق صيغة المجموع اللانهائي بعد التحقق من شرطها.","En":"Apply the infinite-sum formula after checking its condition."}],"Title":{"Ar":"تمييز التقارب وحساب المجموع النهائي","En":"Recognize convergence and calculate an infinite geometric sum"},"Points":10,"Options":[{"Reason":{"Ar":"8 مجموع أول حدين فقط، وباقي الحدود موجبة.","En":"8 is the first two terms only; later terms are positive."},"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","IsCorrect":false,"LatexCode":"8"},{"Reason":null,"ErrorType":"","IsCorrect":true,"LatexCode":"9"},{"Reason":{"Ar":"12 ينتج عن استعمال النسبة 1/2 بدلاً من 1/3.","En":"12 results from using ratio 1/2 instead of 1/3."},"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","IsCorrect":false,"LatexCode":"12"},{"Reason":{"Ar":"18 ينتج عن القسمة على النسبة بدلاً من واحد ناقص النسبة.","En":"18 divides by the ratio instead of one minus the ratio."},"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","IsCorrect":false,"LatexCode":"18"}],"StageId":3,"Question":{"Ar":"احسب مجموع المتسلسلة اللانهائية $6+2+\\frac23+\\frac29+\\cdots$.","En":"Compute the infinite sum $6+2+\\frac23+\\frac29+\\cdots$."},"Solution":{"Idea":{"Ar":"نسبة الحدود المتتالية ثلث، ولذلك تتقارب المتسلسلة الهندسية.","En":"The consecutive-term ratio is one third, so the geometric series converges."},"Unit":{"Ar":"بلا وحدة قياس","En":"Dimensionless"},"Steps":[{"Ar":"الحد الأول 6، والنسبة $r=2/6=1/3$.","En":"The first term is 6 and the ratio is $r=2/6=1/3$."},{"Ar":"بما أن $|r|<1$، نستعمل قانون المجموع الهندسي اللانهائي.","En":"Since $|r|<1$, use the infinite geometric sum formula."},{"Ar":"$S=\\frac6{1-1/3}=\\frac6{2/3}=9$.","En":"$S=\\frac6{1-1/3}=\\frac6{2/3}=9$."}],"Result":{"Ar":"$9$","En":"$9$"},"CommonError":{"Ar":"لا تستعمل النسبة العكسية.","En":"Do not use the inverse ratio."},"FormulaLatex":"S=\\frac{a_1}{1-r}\\quad(|r|<1)","Substitution":{"Ar":"$r=1/3,\\quad S=\\frac6{1-1/3}=9$","En":"$r=1/3,\\quad S=\\frac6{1-1/3}=9$"},"Verification":{"Ar":"$9-9/3=6$","En":"$9-9/3=6$"}},"TrackIds":[12],"CategoryId":23,"PrimarySkillId":113,"DifficultyLevel":1,"SecondarySkillIds":[]}$mw$::jsonb,$mw${"DifficultyLevel":1,"Hints":[{"Ar":"استخرج النسبة بقسمة الثاني على الأول.","En":"Find the ratio by dividing the second term by the first."},{"Ar":"طبّق صيغة المجموع اللانهائي بعد التحقق من شرطها.","En":"Apply the infinite-sum formula after checking its condition."}],"Solution":{"Idea":{"Ar":"نسبة الحدود المتتالية ثلث، ولذلك تتقارب المتسلسلة الهندسية.","En":"The consecutive-term ratio is one third, so the geometric series converges."},"Unit":{"Ar":"بلا وحدة قياس","En":"Dimensionless"},"Steps":[{"Ar":"الحد الأول 6، والنسبة $r=2/6=1/3$.","En":"The first term is 6 and the ratio is $r=2/6=1/3$."},{"Ar":"بما أن $|r|<1$، نستعمل قانون المجموع الهندسي اللانهائي.","En":"Since $|r|<1$, use the infinite geometric sum formula."},{"Ar":"$S=\\frac6{1-1/3}=\\frac6{2/3}=9$.","En":"$S=\\frac6{1-1/3}=\\frac6{2/3}=9$."}],"Result":{"Ar":"$9$","En":"$9$"},"CommonError":{"Ar":"لا تستعمل النسبة العكسية.","En":"Do not use the inverse ratio."},"FormulaLatex":"S=\\frac{a_1}{1-r}\\quad(|r|<1)","Substitution":{"Ar":"$r=1/3,\\quad S=\\frac6{1-1/3}=9$","En":"$r=1/3,\\quad S=\\frac6{1-1/3}=9$"},"Verification":{"Ar":"$9-9/3=6$","En":"$9-9/3=6$"}},"Distractors":[{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"8 مجموع أول حدين فقط، وباقي الحدود موجبة.","En":"8 is the first two terms only; later terms are positive."},"Order":1},{"ErrorType":"","Reason":null,"Order":2},{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"12 ينتج عن استعمال النسبة 1/2 بدلاً من 1/3.","En":"12 results from using ratio 1/2 instead of 1/3."},"Order":3},{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"18 ينتج عن القسمة على النسبة بدلاً من واحد ناقص النسبة.","En":"18 divides by the ratio instead of one minus the ratio."},"Order":4}]}$mw$,$mw$نسبة الحدود المتتالية ثلث، ولذلك تتقارب المتسلسلة الهندسية.

$S=\frac{a_1}{1-r}\quad(|r|<1)$

1. الحد الأول 6، والنسبة $r=2/6=1/3$.

2. بما أن $|r|<1$، نستعمل قانون المجموع الهندسي اللانهائي.

3. $S=\frac6{1-1/3}=\frac6{2/3}=9$.

$r=1/3,\quad S=\frac6{1-1/3}=9$

$9$ بلا وحدة قياس

$9-9/3=6$

لا تستعمل النسبة العكسية.$mw$,$mw$The consecutive-term ratio is one third, so the geometric series converges.

$S=\frac{a_1}{1-r}\quad(|r|<1)$

1. The first term is 6 and the ratio is $r=2/6=1/3$.

2. Since $|r|<1$, use the infinite geometric sum formula.

3. $S=\frac6{1-1/3}=\frac6{2/3}=9$.

$r=1/3,\quad S=\frac6{1-1/3}=9$

$9$ Dimensionless

$9-9/3=6$

Do not use the inverse ratio.$mw$),
